format 1
adapter curriculum 1
unit: inside-the-atom

objective u1-change-protons
statement: Know that changing the number of protons changes the element.
misconception: An atom stays the same element when it gains or loses a proton.

item u1-l3-choice-gain-two
type: choice
difficulty: 2
surfaces: practice
surfaces: checkpoint
surfaces: review
references: ref-openstax-chem-ch2

prompt:
    A carbon atom gains 2 protons. What is it now?

figure: elements-by-protons

options:
    {"id":"oxygen","label":"Oxygen"}
    {"id":"carbon","label":"Still carbon","note":"Carbon has 6 protons. With 8 it is a different element."}
    {"id":"nitrogen","label":"Nitrogen","note":"Nitrogen has 7 protons. That is only one more."}

answer: oxygen

explanation:
    6 protons plus 2 is 8 protons, and 8 protons is oxygen.

item u1-l3-choice-lose-proton
type: choice
difficulty: 2
surfaces: lesson
surfaces: practice
surfaces: review
references: ref-openstax-chem-ch2

prompt:
    An oxygen atom has 8 protons. It loses one proton. What is it now?

figure: elements-by-protons

options:
    {"id":"nitrogen","label":"Nitrogen"}
    {"id":"oxygen","label":"Still oxygen","note":"Oxygen has 8 protons. With 7, the atom is a different element."}
    {"id":"carbon","label":"Carbon","note":"Carbon has 6 protons. That would mean losing two."}

answer: nitrogen

explanation:
    8 protons take away 1 is 7 protons, and 7 protons is nitrogen.

item u1-l3-tom-gain-proton
type: true_or_myth
surfaces: lesson
surfaces: practice
surfaces: review
references: ref-openstax-chem-ch2

statement:
    A carbon atom that gains one proton is still carbon.

answer: myth

explanation:
    Myth. Carbon has 6 protons. With one more it has 7, and 7 protons is nitrogen. Change the protons and you change the element.

item u1-x-proton-change
type: choice
difficulty: 2
surfaces: practice
surfaces: checkpoint
surfaces: review
references: ref-openstax-chem-ch2

prompt:
    A nitrogen atom has 7 protons. It gains one proton. What happens?

options:
    {"id":"oxygen","label":"It becomes oxygen, a different element"}
    {"id":"nitrogen","label":"It is still nitrogen, just heavier","note":"The protons decide the element, so adding one changes the element."}
    {"id":"carbon","label":"It becomes carbon","note":"Carbon has fewer protons, not more."}

answer: oxygen

explanation:
    7 protons plus 1 is 8 protons, and 8 protons is oxygen.

item u1-x-true-change-protons
type: true_or_myth
surfaces: practice
surfaces: checkpoint
surfaces: review
references: ref-openstax-chem-ch2

statement:
    If you change the number of protons in an atom, it becomes a different element.

answer: true

explanation:
    True. The number of protons tells you the element, so changing it changes the element.
